WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.800 line:78% position:50% align:center
In one second, light could circle Earth
seven and a half times.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:09.200 line:78% position:50% align:center
In a vacuum, it travels nearly
300,000 kilometers every second.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:13.600 line:78% position:50% align:center
Earth to the Moon takes only
about 1.28 seconds.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:19.500 line:78% position:50% align:center
Sunlight needs about 8 minutes 20 seconds
to reach us.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.800 line:78% position:50% align:center
In one year, light covers
9.46 trillion kilometers.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.300 line:78% position:50% align:center
Yet even at that speed, Proxima Centauri
is still 4.25 years away.
